error[E0277]: `Vec<u8>` is not ordered: the ordering operators are answered over the integers of 16 bits and wider, the floats, text, dates, timestamps and decimals
  --> tests/ui/order_index_on_bytes.rs:18:13
   |
18 |     digest: Encrypted<OreTerm<Vec<u8>>>,
   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ no ordering operator over this type
   |
   = help: the trait `Ordered` is not implemented for `Vec<u8>`
   = note: `Lt`, `Lte`, `Gt`, `Gte` and `Between` take `u16` to `u128`, `i16` to `i128`, `f32`, `f64`, a `String`, or a `value::Date`, `value::Timestamp` or `value::Decimal`; a `u8`, an `i8` and a `bool` have no order term
   = help: the following other types implement trait `Ordered`:
             f32
             f64
             i128
             i16
             i32
             i64
             stack_encrypt::value::Date
             stack_encrypt::value::Decimal
           and $N others
   = note: required for `OreTerm<Vec<u8>>` to implement `TermSet<Vec<u8>>`
   = note: required for `Encrypted<OreTerm<Vec<u8>>>` to implement `EncryptTarget<Vec<u8>>`

